From: jingledingle521 <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:48:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Mac Settings: back button on QML pages; sidebar inset
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ‹ for pages opened from a list now lives inside QML pages' own
headers (a widget over the page was hidden under it), and hides when a
page is opened any other way. Sidebar rows start further in from their
selection. MAC_TEST_BACK=<page> opens General's list and then that page,
for checking the button without clicking.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KdkdNUmoM62iDwjRop6X5f
